  "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $-1$ and $t$ with $3$ in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x}{2t}-\\frac{3x}{t} & = \\\\ \\frac{6(-1)}{2(3)}-\\frac{3(-1)}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{-6}{6}-\\frac{-3}{3} & = \\\\ -1-(-1) & = \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
